# Cloudflare Pages _redirects.
#
# Path-level rules work here and are applied on every hostname bound to the
# project (measured 2026-08-10: `/probe-redirects-ok /probe-target 301`
# returned 301 on airsonde.com, www.airsonde.com and airsonde-web.pages.dev).
#
# Host-level rules do NOT. A full-URL source such as
#   https://www.airsonde.com/* https://airsonde.com/:splat 301
# is simply never matched — www.airsonde.com kept returning 200 with the
# homepage and no Location header, while path rules in the same file still
# fired. It does not break the other rules; it just does nothing.
#
# So www -> apex has to be a zone-level Redirect Rule in Cloudflare, not a line
# in this file. Add path rules below as the site grows (CF Pages caps this file
# at ~140 rules).

# Capabilities stopped being a top-level section on 2026-08-11 (Joe's六大板块
# IA); its content lives in /about/ now.
/capabilities/* /about/ 301
/capabilities /about/ 301
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Verifying anything on this project: "Active" is not "live".
#
# A deployment shows Active in `wrangler pages deployment list` roughly 40-60s
# before it actually serves everywhere. Curling straight after Active returns
# the PREVIOUS build. That read cost us a wrong conclusion once (we nearly
# reported that the host-form line above poisons the whole file — it does not;
# we had simply measured the old deployment).
#
# So: after pushing, sleep ~25s+, append a cache-buster (?cb=$RANDOM) and take
# the same assertion 2-3 times consistently before believing it. When a reading
# contradicts expectation, suspect propagation before suspecting the code.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

